cell a3z/real DONE -> cortex-retrofit/p30-oracle-a3z-real

READING ORDER -- and the pair is the result, never one limb alone:
  1. tools/compare_arms.py --stopping_rule on real vs shuffled,
     SAME arm.  A paired CI on one side of zero across two
     consecutive non-overlapping windows is the claim.
  2. the read gate's trajectory in cortex_diag.jsonl.  A gate that
     collapses toward zero is the model saying it does not want the
     read -- pre-registered as a legitimate negative, so do not read
     it as a bug.
  3. eval_influence_horizon --channel z --damage donor on the REAL
     limb's checkpoint.  If the trained read does not depend on
     content, that contradicts limb 1 and both need auditing.
  4. a2 answers 'does readable carry exist'.  a3z answers 'does it
     exist in the model that ships'.  They can differ.
